sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor Staff as Administrator / Operator
    participant UI as Web Portal
    participant API as ProductsController
    participant Service as CatalogService
    participant Store as CatalogStore
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database

    %% ==========================================
    %% 1. CREATE PRODUCT DRAFT
    %% ==========================================

    Staff->>+UI: Open Create Product and enter product details

    UI->>+API: Create(productData)
    API->>+Service: CreateProductAsync(productData)

    Service->>+Store: Validate Category and SKU uniqueness
    Store->>+DB: SELECT Category and existing Product by SKU
    DB-->>Store: Category and SKU information
    deactivate DB

    Store-->>Service: Validation data
    deactivate Store

    alt Valid Product information

        Service->>+Store: AddProduct(Draft), AddPrice(), SaveChangesAsync()

        Store->>+DB: INSERT Product and ProductPrice in transaction
        DB-->>Store: Product Draft created
        deactivate DB

        Store-->>Service: Created Product
        deactivate Store

        Service-->>API: ProductResult (Draft)

    else Invalid Category, duplicate SKU or invalid data

        Service-->>API: Validation or conflict error

    end

    deactivate Service

    API-->>UI: Creation response
    deactivate API

    UI-->>Staff: Display Draft Product or error
    deactivate UI

    %% ==========================================
    %% 2. PUBLISH PRODUCT
    %% ==========================================

    opt Product Draft created successfully

        Staff->>+UI: Select Publish Product

        UI->>+API: Publish(productId)
        API->>+Service: PublishProductAsync(productId)

        Service->>+Store: Retrieve Product, Category and active Price
        Store->>+DB: SELECT Product, Category and ProductPrice
        DB-->>Store: Product and related information
        deactivate DB

        Store-->>Service: Product publication data
        deactivate Store

        alt Draft with valid required fields and active Price

            Note over Service,DB: Replacement publication also inactivates<br/>the predecessor in the same transaction

            Service->>+Store: Set Product status to Published and save

            Store->>+DB: UPDATE Product status and publication timestamp
            DB-->>Store: Publication committed
            deactivate DB

            Store-->>Service: Published Product
            deactivate Store

            Service-->>API: ProductResult (Published)

        else Already Published

            Service-->>API: Current Published Product

        else Invalid Product status or missing requirements

            Service-->>API: Publication rejected

        end

        deactivate Service

        API-->>UI: Publication response
        deactivate API

        UI-->>Staff: Display Published Product or error
        deactivate UI

    end